@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ai-owner-is-not-a-github-prerequisite
An AI principal MUST come from a trusted verified Pully/local owner or an explicitly
issued anonymous/default allowance; a request body or shared Guest namespace MUST NOT
mint authority. A principal alone MUST NOT grant a provider credential or paid budget.
GitHub login MUST NOT be required to configure or use every AI connection. Source:
Tavi's 22 Oct 2026 AI-without-GitHub and independent provider-capability instruction.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] ai-runs-retain-their-connection-authority
A provider request, tool action, event and result publication MUST retain the original
owner, provider kind, connection ID and revision. Source retirement or connection
replacement/removal MUST retire captured leases before new authority is published.
Retirement notifications MUST be installed before the corresponding current-state
check and MUST NOT replace it. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct per-user credential/source plan
and 22 Oct approved independent Responses/provider implementation boundaries.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ai-protocol-code-cannot-resolve-secrets
Provider protocol adapters MUST obtain request authorization from the captured
credential capability, which MUST restrict authorization to its exact trusted target
and method. Adapters MUST NOT read environment, CLI homes, another connection's
credential, or choose a private first-party endpoint. Refresh and revocation MUST
remain with credential custody, and credentials MUST NOT enter Debug, output, errors
or analytics. A request factory MUST enforce disabled redirects/proxies and finite
network/body limits. Source: Tavi's 22 Oct explicit provider custody and protocol split.
